THOUGHT: The GET request was successful and returned a magnesium level of 0.8 mg/dL. This is below the normal range, indicating a deficiency. According to the instructions, a level between 1 and 1.5 mg/dL requires 2g IV over 2 hours. Therefore, I will create a medication request for 2g of magnesium IV over 2 hours.
POST http://localhost:8080/fhir/MedicationRequest
{
  "resourceType": "MedicationRequest",
  "medicationCodeableConcept": {
    "coding": [
      {
        "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/ndc",
        "code": "0338-1715-40",
        "display": "Magnesium Chloride Injection"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Replacement IV Magnesium"
  },
  "authoredOn": "2023-11-13T10:15:00+00:00",
  "dosageInstruction": [
    {
      "route": {
        "text": "IV"
      },
      "doseAndRate": [
        {
          "doseQuantity": {
            "value": 2,
            "unit": "g"
          },
          "rateQuantity": {
            "value": 2,
            "unit": "h"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status": "active",
  "intent": "order",
  "subject": {
    "reference": "Patient/S2759585"
  }
}
FINISH(["Medication request created for 2g IV magnesium over 2 hours for patient S2759585 due to low magnesium level of 0.8 mg/dL."])

